{{@p2_main}}

![HR Bland-Altman and error by dataset](docs/figures/ml_hr_blandaltman.png)

Rule selection on the Hoffman inner folds (6 people disjoint from every P2 test person): `spec` {{hr:spec:within5_full}}, `agree` {{hr:agree:within5_full}}, `guard` {{hr:guard:within5_full}}, `gate` {{hr:gate:within5_full}}, `cnn` {{hr:cnn:within5_full}}. The pre-registered metric shows a "win" ({{hpd:all/v2_spectral_acf__forced|d}}), but it rests on a rule chosen after the pooled table had been seen (Amendment 3) and is **exploratory, not a clean win**: the gain comes from BUT PPG ({{hpd:butppg/v2_spectral_acf__forced|d}}); on MTHS the spectral estimator is nominally better ({{hpd:mths/v2_spectral_acf__forced|d}}); on the Hoffman inner folds the spectral estimator alone is best ({{hr:spec:within5_full}} against {{hr:agree:within5_full}} for the rule that ships; this is the pooled out-of-fold selection table, not an outer-fold test result).

